{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "{"id": 559, "depth": 4, "text": ".\n\nI didn't really know much about Iran, but I knew that the Revolutionary Guards were a security force and a force for the protection of the revolution. I could not understand why anyone would go against them. In order to kill Omar, they would have to have the help of the IRGC, the army's elite and elite military force, that was supposed to be protecting them.\n\nI got one last look at the pictures from my trip. I called Youssef's girlfriend. She confirmed that she had seen my picture. She did not want the picture to end up on the internet, so I passed it off to the reporter for a story he had wanted. He passed it to the Lebanese journalist I knew, who sent me an email with the details. He wanted the story. I figured he had enough to give me.\n\nBefore heading back to the States, I stopped by a friend of mine in San Francisco. I told him everything that had happened. He was shocked and called the FBI immediately. When he got the FBI involved, it was over. They wanted to talk to me, but I had the pictures and I couldn't talk to them about where I'd been. They told me to give them a call when I got to", "seed_id": 111, "token_count": 256, "model": "pythia-2.8b", "domain": "news"}
{"id": 560, "depth": 0, "text": "(CNN)#UporDown? That's the trending question on social media, thanks to a photo of a cat coming down some stairs. Or is it going up some stairs? (And you thought you were done with this kind of optical illusion free-for-all after #TheDress.) The picture was apparently uploaded on Imgur a few days ago and has caught fire thanks to a post on the website 9gag.com. Some people are noting the apparent motion of the cat. Others are commenting about the construction of the stairs. (Nobody has mentioned that some cats we could name would be more likely to stop in the middle of the steps and play with a mousie.) Of course, where there's public debate, there are advertisers waiting to take advantage of the situation. Taxes? Now, those are REALLY confusing.", "seed_id": 112, "token_count": 173, "model": "pythia-2.8b", "domain": "news"}
{"id": 561, "depth": 1, "text": " So, are you ready to debate a tax proposal that was on the ballots in Ohio and Washington D.C., respectively? If you don't want to, I'm not going to force you to. I'm pretty sure it wouldn't be in your best interest.\n\nThe cat is called \"Ted\" and the catwalk is called \"Cascade\"\n\nIt is kind of amusing. Here is a video of this odd event:", "seed_id": 112, "token_count": 91, "model": "pythia-2.8b", "domain": "news"}
